Novox patch for whisper.cpp v1.8.3 (the assert is unchanged through v1.9.5 / master, 2026-10;
upstream PR ggml-org/whisper.cpp#4096 proposes a similar fix). Applied by FetchContent in
plugin/CMakeLists.txt through plugin/patches/git-apply-once.cmake.

With DTW token timestamps on, each decoded window is aligned against its own audio tokens
(n_frames/2, 20 ms each). A window that advanced under 160 ms (a segment ending at <|0.14|>,
or a 110 ms sliver at the end of the file) has fewer audio tokens than the median filter is
wide (7), and WHISPER_ASSERT(filter_width < a->ne[2]) aborted the process: inside a DAW that
takes down the host. Reproduced on CSD en023b.wav (seek_delta 14) and en012a.wav (11 frames
left). The filter now runs whenever reflect padding fits (half-width < length) and is skipped
otherwise, like openai-whisper's timing.py. Windows under 2 audio tokens skip DTW entirely
(their 1D alignment matrix would trip dtw_and_backtrace's ggml_n_dims assert); their tokens
keep t_dtw = -1. Windows of 8+ audio tokens take exactly the old path.

diff --git a/src/whisper.cpp b/src/whisper.cpp
index 5b6e4b4..2d2d547 100644
--- a/src/whisper.cpp
+++ b/src/whisper.cpp
@@ -8769,7 +8769,20 @@ static void median_filter(struct ggml_tensor * dst , const struct ggml_tensor *
         return;
     }
     int filter_width = ((median_filter_user_data *) userdata)->filter_width;
-    WHISPER_ASSERT(filter_width < a->ne[2]);
+    // A window that advanced under 8 audio tokens (160 ms: a segment ending at <|0.14|>, or
+    // the last sliver of a file) used to abort the whole process here. Reflect padding only
+    // needs the half-width to fit, so filter whenever it does and otherwise pass the values
+    // through unfiltered, as openai-whisper's timing.py median_filter does.
+    if (filter_width/2 >= a->ne[2]) {
+        for (int64_t i = 0; i < a->ne[0]; ++i) {
+            for (int64_t j = 0; j < a->ne[1]; ++j) {
+                for (int64_t k = 0; k < a->ne[2]; ++k) {
+                    whisper_set_f32_nd(dst, i, j, k, 0, whisper_get_f32_nd(a, i, j, k, 0));
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        return;
+    }
     WHISPER_ASSERT(filter_width % 2);
     WHISPER_ASSERT(ggml_n_dims(a) == 3);
     WHISPER_ASSERT(a->type == GGML_TYPE_F32);
@@ -8815,6 +8828,13 @@ static void whisper_exp_compute_token_level_timestamps_dtw(
     WHISPER_ASSERT(n_frames <= n_audio_ctx * 2);
     WHISPER_ASSERT(ctx->params.dtw_aheads_preset != WHISPER_AHEADS_NONE);
 
+    // Under 2 audio tokens (a window that advanced under 40 ms) there is nothing to align, and
+    // the alignment matrix would collapse to one dimension, which dtw_and_backtrace asserts
+    // against. Leave t_dtw at -1 (callers fall back to t0/t1) instead of aborting.
+    if (n_frames/2 < 2) {
+        return;
+    }
+
     // FIXME: Allocating mem everytime we call this func
     // Our ggml buffer should be pre-allocated somewhere during init and reused
     // when we call this function
